// title: PieChart - Exposure Level Onboarded Devices · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceInfo
// purpose: This query visualizes the onboarded devices and their exposure level in a PieChart. The higher the exposure level of a device, the more likely it is to be exploited.
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Vulnerability%20Management/Visualization%20-%20ExposureLevels.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
DeviceInfo
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where OnboardingStatus == "Onboarded"
| summarize arg_max(Timestamp, *) by DeviceId
| summarize Total = count() by ExposureLevel
| render piechart with(title="Overview Exposure Level")
